# Day 9 – Seasonal Sales Trend Analysis

## Objective
Identify how sales fluctuate across the year — which months and quarters
drive the most revenue, spot peak and low periods, and understand what's
selling during those peaks.

## What I Built
- Added `OrderMonth`, `OrderMonthNumber`, and `OrderQuarter` columns in
  Power Query, derived from Order Date
- Sorted `OrderMonth` by `OrderMonthNumber` so charts display January →
  December in correct calendar order instead of alphabetically
- Built a dashboard with:
  - A line chart of Total Sales by Month (main trend visual)
  - A bar chart of Total Sales by Quarter (zoomed-out seasonal view)
  - A Top N table showing best-selling products in the peak month vs. the
    lowest month
  - KPI cards for Best Month and Worst Month by sales
  - (If data spans multiple years) A Year slicer to compare seasonality
    year over year rather than blending years together

